  "notes": ["The empty-grid source replay retains the initial area hit and forks just before a new seat-1 B on visit 186. Extra cells, if any, are appended to the original free lists before that press.","The first area requests 4 HP from the new bomb and removes its only 1 HP. The original next visit reaches the zero-HP branch with a nonexpired timer.","Carrier allocation and shape binding are separate. At the second area's initializer both prior shapes still occupy their cells; the new shape requires an additional free slot.","The two areas keep the same actor credit and amount record but different carrier and shape cells, and tokens 2 and 4. A stored parent address is not a lifetime identity: the original bomb cell was reused.","With both resources available, token 4 reaches both actors again, each from tier 0. The self hit changes only received damage, not the owner's ally or opponent credit.","The fork stops after both area carriers retire. The replay does not qualify other setups, further B presses, rendering, hardware, or native gameplay."],
